codeBraceT -- SEQ 512 (Tony, 2026-11-02): aCTionCodE (ruleActions.rtn) captured a code={ } body from its { to the FIRST },
counting no nesting and stepping over no quote, so a } in a quoted string, a } closing a braced block (braceInCode) or a }
in a comment (KANT-40 / F-86) ended the body early. The define holding it died -- naming its first healthy action,
bear-trap 32 -- and the parse ABANDONED the rest of the file at exit 0. PRE-REGISTERED ON TRUNK, born red.

Defines are always the old road's, so there is no new-road twin: BC-3 is the control (a { in a string never broke).
One process; each row has its own define, a stderr sentinel right after the define (absent = that define abandoned the
file), then its calls under a `BC <row>` stdout line.

ROWS
BC-3  control: print "{" then 7 -> { 7.
BIC   braceInCode's repro: bcFirst prints 3; bcBad's braced arm sits under a false if, so 5 alone.
BC-1  a } inside a quoted string: } 7.
BC-2  a braced nested block under a true if: 1 2 5.
BC-4  a } in a // comment -- balanced (code={ x }) then a lone }: 6 8. The ruling's scan skips quoted strings and counts
      depth; a lone } in a comment needs the comment skipped too, and this row says whether it is.
